{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion","id":123107,"title":"Cursed Necropolis DC Discussion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-01T06:38:25-07:00","id":123107,"title":"Cursed Necropolis DC Discussion","content":"<b>The latest supplement for <i>Mummy: the Curse</i> has been released to KS backers! Let's talk about all the goodies here.</b> <hr /><br /> First up, in the SAS there is an Arisen who has an utterance, Smite the Heavens, which is not given stats yet in any <i>Mummy</i> book. There's a lot of tantalizing bits about the Deceived in this book, too.<br /> <br /> Also, the photographic rendition of myself that I paid $300 for in the KS is on page 50. I'm pretty happy but I do have to say that 1) I wasn't wearing a suit, 2) it looks like my smirk was flattened out to expressionless lips, and 3) my stretched ear lobes are colored in and my pierced septum isn't pierced. That last one is kind of a bummer. What, there aren't any Mummies with piercings? There can't be one Arisen who has their nose pierced? That's what I paid for, isn't it? :\\","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T07:07:54-07:00","id":123121,"title":"","content":"I'm not done with it yet but my biggest question is still not answered yet. Has anyone else seen any mention of it in their reading of the book?<br /> <br /> Unease Sybaris. Being within [Sekhem] miles of a Mummy or their Tomb for 24 hours+ causes Unease Sybaris. The level of Unease is Memory minus Sekhem.<br /> <br /> Several of these Mummies (especially the Khent-henu) have low Memory traits, even a rating 1!<br /> <br /> Because of the Heka flows in D.C. Descents are slower.<br /> <br /> When you wake up you can last at Sekhem 10 for 2+ days. that's more than 24 hours for those who are counting...<br /> <br /> With so many Mummies in close proximity, shouldn't the whole city be in near constant Unease Sybaris as someone low memory wakes up, floods the place with Madness of Duat for weeks on end (weeks equal to Sekhem at the time the Unease started) for miles and miles? is there something that explains how this Sybaris affects the city? If a place if afflicted with Sybaris like that for potentially 2 hundred of year you'd expect there to be...something about dealing with it?<br /> <br /> it;s one fo the things I personally find hard to reconcile with the concept of Nomes and a society that stays in the same place for extended periods in large numbers. Madness for a few weeks every decade if there is one local Mummy can be explained away. The affects of that with many times the frequency? The affects of the Guildmaster ranked Afinities buffing the ability to make money and the option to trade Physical or Morality traits for wealth within miles of the Guildmasters is dealt with by the text so I know the authors are paying attention to these kinds of things so I'm wondering if there's somewhere in the book that deals with the Sybaris issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T07:37:08-07:00","id":123141,"title":"","content":"Traditional White Wolf system wonkiness. Either Unease Sybaris or mummy society doesn't really work as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T08:14:02-07:00","id":123161,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying this as a cop-out nor am I done reading the book (obviously), but I think the side-bar &quot;A Word on Liberties&quot; addresses the sybaris effects on a meta level. They, basically, say that DC isn't as bad of a place as it used to be, but in the World of Darkness it actually is worse than it ever was.<br /> <br /> The authors definitely did try to cover as many questions as they could, and I give them props. The Storyteller's chapter is killer - including talk of Mummies interacting with other supernaturals (or, at least, vampires, and then why Mummies and other supernaturals might not pay mutual attention to each other)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T08:15:26-07:00","id":123164,"title":"","content":"I had something in there to deal with Unease Sybaris and how they interact with nomes; it appears to have slipped out, so I'll see if I can't get it put back in. I realize you don't find the answer particularly palatable, Christian, but the answer to &quot; how do guild and nomes even work with no memory&quot; is &quot;cults and talismans&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T08:29:11-07:00","id":123175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion#post123107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The latest supplement for <i>Mummy: the Curse</i> has been released to KS backers! Let's talk about all the goodies here.</b> <hr /><br /> First up, in the SAS there is an Arisen who has an utterance, Smite the Heavens, which is not given stats yet in any <i>Mummy</i> book. There's a lot of tantalizing bits about the Deceived in this book, too.<br /> Also, the photographic rendition of myself that I paid $300 for in the KS is on page 50. I'm pretty happy but I do have to say that 1) I wasn't wearing a suit, 2) it looks like my smirk was flattened out to expressionless lips, and 3) my stretched ear lobes are colored in and my pierced septum isn't pierced. That last one is kind of a bummer. What, there aren't any Mummies with piercings? There can't be one Arisen who has their nose pierced? That's what I paid for, isn't it? :\\</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really enjoying it so far <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Excellent to hear you're in the book! Regarding the change in costume and minor physical amendments - I believe it's to keep your image within the context of the setting. So for instance, I've appeared in Anarchs Unbound, but not in the suit I was wearing for the photoshoot. Instead I'm in an historical piece, wearing a robe and looking significantly more deathly than in reality. I think we've got to accept (and be happy with, hopefully!) an artist taking us and moulding us into their vision of what a character resembling us would look like in the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T09:04:49-07:00","id":123201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=123164#post123164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had something in there to deal with Unease Sybaris and how they interact with nomes; it appears to have slipped out, so I'll see if I can't get it put back in. I realize you don't find the answer particularly palatable, Christian, but the answer to &quot; how do guild and nomes even work with no memory&quot; is &quot;cults and talismans&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Good to know there was something on Unease <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, seemed odd to be missing considering the Guildmaster Affinities were in there, you guys were clearly considering the wider applications of their powers.<br /> <br /> The Memory issue is...still one I struggle with at times. The importance of Cults in Mummy society is obviously huge. I know the texts obviously focus on the Mummies (and so they should) but that kind of made the individuals in Cults seem less important. The importance of Cults thus raises the importance of things like Unease Sybaris because the visions and madness and fear that Sybaris causes on a wide scale is obviously feeds into creating people who are actually susceptible to recruitment or spurred on to forming a cult in the first place.<br /> <br /> Talismans...I may have to go back and reread their section in Guildhalls but the Talismanic Record never felt like a huge thing in that book, I vaguely remember it only being mentioned in one instance and no real discussion of how important they were or what they actually let people do. This book does make it clearer, the entirety of the Khent-henu rely almost solely on their Talismans to allow them to function on the scale of history that they do. Talismans are thus, demonstrably, bigger and more important than a small entry in a splat book implied. Though they then do start to erode the importance of actual Memory...if you can run a project as complicated and rapidly evolving as building a Geomantic City through a Talisman then you'd need some serious reason to need to know more about your past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T09:32:43-07:00","id":123221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=123164#post123164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had something in there to deal with Unease Sybaris and how they interact with nomes; it appears to have slipped out, so I'll see if I can't get it put back in. I realize you don't find the answer particularly palatable, Christian, but the answer to &quot; how do guild and nomes even work with no memory&quot; is &quot;cults and talismans&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an answer I can work with; and I've alread changed things in my Mummy setting so as to make things more satisfying for me. And I appreciate your effort!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T10:17:15-07:00","id":123257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=123201#post123201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Memory issue is...still one I struggle with at times. The importance of Cults in Mummy society is obviously huge. I know the texts obviously focus on the Mummies (and so they should) but that kind of made the individuals in Cults seem less important. The importance of Cults thus raises the importance of things like Unease Sybaris because the visions and madness and fear that Sybaris causes on a wide scale is obviously feeds into creating people who are actually susceptible to recruitment or spurred on to forming a cult in the first place.<br /> <br /> Talismans...I may have to go back and reread their section in Guildhalls but the Talismanic Record never felt like a huge thing in that book, I vaguely remember it only being mentioned in one instance and no real discussion of how important they were or what they actually let people do. This book does make it clearer, the entirety of the Khent-henu rely almost solely on their Talismans to allow them to function on the scale of history that they do. Talismans are thus, demonstrably, bigger and more important than a small entry in a splat book implied. Though they then do start to erode the importance of actual Memory...if you can run a project as complicated and rapidly evolving as building a Geomantic City through a Talisman then you'd need some serious reason to need to know more about your past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its fair to say that Mummy has some elements that in the Core did cause some issues. <br /> <br /> The Memory aspect of the game seemed to screw over the larger idea of Guild Structure and Status for example. Not to mention the idea of the Guilds being long-lasting World-spanning organizations when Mummy's themselves are very rare supernatural creatures. Likewise, Unease Sybaris seemed needed to explain how Mummy's build cults so easily but at the same time had...problematic implications for the idea of Nomes. Cults were treated very much as a resource or a merit block, rather then basically the backbone of Mummy culture. <br /> <br /> These issues have been addressed to some degree in the splat books. <br /> <br /> Guildhalls did a decent (not fantastic, a lot of the following is inferred, hinted at and suggested rather then outright stated) job of getting across the idea that the modern form of the Guilds is very much a macro-grouping of allied cults doing the dirty work (often without knowing the Guild even exists as a larger entity). Likewise it stressed the idea that while Guilds are global they are at least regionally divergent in verity and approach e.g. contrast the Maa-Kep of South America with Europe. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile the Arisen masters of these Cults correspond to set Guild policy, aims and methods and sort out things like status via long-range methods (supernatural or mundane) and usually only within regional groupings of the Guild in question. With actually face to face meetings for Guild business being rare (once a decade for the Maa-Kep of Europe for example) or due to important business e.g. Trials. <br /> <br /> Multi-Guild stuff seems to only occur in the larger Nomes or for specific regional purposes. <br /> <br /> Likewise, Guildhalls provided a few more avenues for Memory retention and progression and actually made the idea of progressive Memory gain over multiple descents much more viable via Talismans. <br /> <br /> DC seems from what people are saying (I have yet to read past the introduction) to make how Nomes are organized and function make more sense and just generally be a more valid idea then was presented in the Core book. If Neall can get the Nome feature that deals with Unease Sybaris back in I'd say it did a pretty good job of giving yet another reason why Arisen might form Nomes and congregate around certain areas. Lesson the negative aspects of Unease Sybaris while providing steady cult recruitment targets seems pretty awesome. <br /> <br /> In general all the Mummy splat books so far have done a good job of playing up the importance of cults and demonstrating the myriad roles they fill in Arisen society. <br /> <br /> My is in my top 3 NWoD games (along with Vampire and Demon, it edged out Promethean) and its got a lot of strong points. However, the lines organization of info and content is its biggest weakness (perhaps closely followed by it being in the WoD 1.0 system). Half the stuff (if not volume then focus/emphasis) I mentioned above really should have been in the Core. As CAS has said it suffers from the very limited page count it got. <br /> <br /> Still, with each new release I feel Mummy becomes a better game and I feel that ST's have an easier time running the game and a wider variety of players can be hooked into it. I can see some people criticizing the game and taking issue with having to buy at least 3/4 extra books on top of the Core to get the &quot;complete&quot; game, but I'm not one of them. <br /> <br /> \u200bAll in all, I'm glad we have more Mummy content with this book and that the game and setting continue to get support, get fleshed out and receive refinement for the few snags it had at its initial release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T11:36:38-07:00","id":123308,"title":"","content":"The organization of information makes it feel hoarded sometimes. Definitely requires some close and repeated reading, which is both a strength and a weakness. This book continued the pattern.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I <i>really </i>liked the character writeups in this book, especially Hebeny, Rashida, the White Jackal, and Sedge. The way they fit together helps a nome make sense, but the individuals alone fleshed out the potential of the line for me. Same goes for the example mortals. There were discussions in a few of those writeups about sahus changing based on Memory levels that I didn't remember from the core, but I can't tell how much of it is new and how much I just skimmed over or forgot the first time. <br /> <br /> The whole thing made me nostalgic for living in the district. Writers worked in a lot of authentic detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T15:53:07-07:00","id":123459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=123201#post123201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talismans...I may have to go back and reread their section in Guildhalls but the Talismanic Record never felt like a huge thing in that book, I vaguely remember it only being mentioned in one instance and no real discussion of how important they were or what they actually let people do. This book does make it clearer, the entirety of the Khent-henu rely almost solely on their Talismans to allow them to function on the scale of history that they do. Talismans are thus, demonstrably, bigger and more important than a small entry in a splat book implied. Though they then do start to erode the importance of actual Memory...if you can run a project as complicated and rapidly evolving as building a Geomantic City through a Talisman then you'd need some serious reason to need to know more about your past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talismans have two serious flaws: One, they're actual physical pieces of your memory, and if you lose the talisman somehow and it doesn't occur to you to resurrect around it, you've lost that tremendous crutch you lean on. Two, it provides the actual physical data of what occurs, but there's absolutely zero emotional import behind it - you're making decisions based on what is, essentially, a Wikipedia entry covering your life. It dissociates mummies from human emotions and events in a way that journals - an accurate recounting of your day's trials and emotions - doesn't. There's no emotional context whatsoever. <br /> <br /> Ask Sabola what happens when somebody steals your Talisman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Writers worked in a lot of authentic detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>That means everything. Thank you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T23:56:52-07:00","id":123634,"title":"","content":"Is there a reason she (Sabola) doesn't use <i>kepher</i> to hunt it down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T06:45:23-07:00","id":123751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=123634#post123634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason she (Sabola) doesn't use <i>kepher</i> to hunt it down?</div> </div> </div> </div> She isn't aware that it exists, ergo it's hard to track. It doesn't register to her any more than nearby kepher would (unless her Sekhem is wiped from it somehow) and she's too addled to really know what she's missing. Such is the price of relying on mementos. I implied that Sedge was behind her current state, but I left the hows and the whys up to STs. For all I know the Aegis Kai Doru have it halfway across the world right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T11:14:06-07:00","id":123884,"title":"","content":"Well, hats off gents.<br /> <br /> I'm only half way through this book and I can honestly say its gone into the top 5 supplement books for any NWoD line I've read.<br /> <br /> Its pipped Guildhalls for me by a long stretch. Feels much more cohesive and uniform then Guildhalls (due to 2 writers verses 5/6 I guess) and I actually find it more evocative then the Core (the NPC's are all fantastic and really have widened some of my ideas about Mummy characters in general) in a lot of places. Plus the Deceived stuff makes me giddy. <br /> <br /> Really awesome job on this one. Rio is going to have a lot to live up to. If the line can keep this quality up over Deceived, Sothis Ascends and Dreams of Avarice it might knock Vampire off its top spot of being my favorite game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T12:28:04-07:00","id":123932,"title":"","content":"I thought it was a really nice idea for a character who's senile to that sort of extent to show up - the whole Old Age metaphor and all that. She's probably my favourite NPC from the book.<br /> <br /> And she's <i>still</i> really scary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T18:34:03-07:00","id":124189,"title":"","content":"Not that this is a music thread, but anyone got some soundtrack ideas for this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T22:39:48-07:00","id":124303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent to hear you're in the book! Regarding the change in costume and minor physical amendments - I believe it's to keep your image within the context of the setting. So for instance, I've appeared in Anarchs Unbound, but not in the suit I was wearing for the photoshoot. Instead I'm in an historical piece, wearing a robe and looking significantly more deathly than in reality. I think we've got to accept (and be happy with, hopefully!) an artist taking us and moulding us into their vision of what a character resembling us would look like in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm very happy I made the decision - I have no regrets. I understand adding the suit, I guess I just didn't see a reason to conceal my piercings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That means everything. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Serious high praise for the book. Between the <i>Mummy</i> core, <i>Guildhalls, </i><i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i>, and <i>Demon: the Descent</i> I think this supplement is the best nWoD product Onyx Path has released. I feel like I could do the city justice as a setting (I've never been there), the characters and plots are interesting, the adventure is cool, but most of all I just like the writing. You gave a lot of thought to the implications of <i>Mummy</i>'s magic in their world, but just the actual writing itself I like, too! It's concise, humorous at parts, and just very warm and informative. I really feel like you've crammed more into the 80 pages than I would've guessed possible.<br /> <br /> Regarding Sabola, won't her Memory reset to 3 the next time she awakens from Duat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T08:49:10-07:00","id":124529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=124303#post124303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Sabola, won't her Memory reset to 3 the next time she awakens from Duat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. If she drops to 0, it'll reset to 1, but it won't rise to 3 unless someone takes her around the city and she generates Sebayt experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T11:58:09-07:00","id":124648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=124529#post124529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. If she drops to 0, it'll reset to 1, but it won't rise to 3 unless someone takes her around the city and she generates Sebayt experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. I reread the bit that I had misunderstood in the core, which I now realize says that a Mummy, upon returning to Duat, will lose a dot of Memory unless it would bring her below 3. I thought that meant that the Judges were cool with lashing their minds until a certain point but didn't want them too broken, which didn't really mesh with the rest of the setting's mood or Sothic history to me, which is why I had inadvertently house-ruled Memory to function the way it turns out it was written to begin with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T09:59:12-07:00","id":125215,"title":"","content":"I have a question Neall...<br /> <br /> (I'm only on page 92 out of 119 so I apologize if this is answered later in the book)<br /> <br /> With the Washington Monument damage the effect of the geomancy of Washington is to double the time between descent rolls for Arisen inside the beltway so long as their Sekhem is above 2.<br /> <br /> Considering the Monument is supposed to be finished in its repairs on the 12th of May 2014 (10 days from now) I was wondering if it has a different effect on the Arisen inside the beltway when fully repaired?<br /> <br /> If so what would you say the effect is?<br /> <br /> I'm just curious in case I want to run a chronicle set after the repairs are finished but before Seb-Hetchet rises (or is found at least).<br /> <br /> Alternatively if one wants to run a chronicle set after the monument has been repaired AND Seb-Hetchet has returned and done any geomancy necessary to make sure its working properly (if one decides he's not doing the opposite given the sample adventure).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 05-04-2014, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T12:16:32-07:00","id":126036,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on CN: DC in no particular order:<br /> <br /> * Back in the Guildhalls adventure, Bes-Mat should have had way more screentime than he did. (Or will have, from an in-universe perspective.) He's a much cooler character in here than the bland conservative Maa-Kep security guy who just hung out in the background, being overshadowed by pretty much everyone else.<br /> <br /> * Unfortunately, this book has a lot of one of my biggest gripes about Mummy: lots of awesome weirdness going on the the fluff and the plot and <i>no rules for it</i><i>.</i> Geomancy, mirages and oases, Dedwen, ritual magic apparently unconnected to Affinities and Utterances, the list goes on.I want systems for creating my own geomantic effects! I want heka and Dedwen and the Word to be actual <i>things</i> with rules of their own, not just Guild-specific flavoring for the mechanics we already have! It's really frustrating to have all this cool, unique stuff in the descriptions and no way to <i>use</i> it more concrete than handwaving. I <i>really</i> hope that we'll see at least some of this in a future supplement.<br /> <br /> * Hebeny is awesome. That is all.<br /> <br /> * Speaking of Hebeny, I note that both he and Seb-Hetchet have the requisite Memory and Pillars to attempt Apotheosis, at least if the lowered Pillar requirements are in effect. Hints for future metaplot?<br /> <br /> * Is it just me, or is Ahm-An Taht one big Doctor Who reference?<br /> <br /> * The art was kind of hit-or-miss. A lot of it was great, but quite a few of the character portraits didn't at <i>all</i> match their descriptions. Seb-Hetchet in particular--his description makes it clear that he's the signature Tef-Aabhi from the core (the classy-looking guy with long hair, a white suit, and a watch; also shown on the cover of this book), but his portrait is some generically scruffy guy with a five o'clock shadow.<br /> <br /> * I'd never considered that the Talismanic Record could serve as a poor man's Memory, but as written, it totally could. Interesting.<br /> <br /> * The Deceived are awesome. Also, apparently astrologers. Is this another facet of their role as masters of Naming? Knowing the secret names of the stars, upon which Fate is written...<br /> <br /> * Also, still no clear indication that the Deceived are actually evil. For all that the book demonizes them when talking about them from the perspective of the Arisen, the actual description of what Hab-Utet is trying to do is pretty ambiguous. I mean, he's described as wanting to &quot;tear down the works of Irem&quot;, but given what we know about what Irem was like, that's not exactly an inherently malevolent goal. (I mean, let's face it: in the world of Mummy, no one's hands are clean, and killing a few endangered animals to make a super-Amkhata is actually pretty tame as apparently &quot;evil&quot; acts go. The ostensible &quot;good guys&quot; in this scenario have done much, much worse.) I'm getting the impression that it would be entirely possible to play a heroic Deceived, even if Hab-Utet turns out to be evil incarnate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T12:44:07-07:00","id":126061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=126036#post126036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts on CN: DC in no particular order:<br /> * Unfortunately, this book has a lot of one of my biggest gripes about Mummy: lots of awesome weirdness going on the the fluff and the plot and <i>no rules for it</i><i>.</i> Geomancy, mirages and oases, Dedwen, ritual magic apparently unconnected to Affinities and Utterances, the list goes on.I want systems for creating my own geomantic effects! I want heka and Dedwen and the Word to be actual <i>things</i> with rules of their own, not just Guild-specific flavoring for the mechanics we already have! It's really frustrating to have all this cool, unique stuff in the descriptions and no way to <i>use</i> it more concrete than handwaving. I <i>really</i> hope that we'll see at least some of this in a future supplement.<br /> ...<br /> * ...I'm getting the impression that it would be entirely possible to play a heroic Deceived, even if Hab-Utet turns out to be evil incarnate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I half-agree on the first point. A lot of interesting stories and plots come from exceptions to the rules. Mummies can't be possessed by ephemeral beings so...what happens when that actually happens? The upcoming <i>Mage</i> update, <i>The Fallen World Chronicles</i>, posits just such Mysteries as the reason Mages even come together as a society in the first place. And the core book does say affinities and utterances are cast through a 'filter' of the guild's magic. On the other hand, I would like some sort of standard by which all this magic is held by so we're not completely blindsided and dumbfounded all the time.<br /> <br /> <i>Book of the Deceived</i> will have rules for playing the Sixth Guild, so you may be able to just play a heroic Deceived. All I can hope for is that, while the Deceived surely have some anti-hero motivations and justifications, they don't overshadow the typical Arisen. They might know more Secret Truths than the latter, but I don't want them to know everything. It's a fine line, but I want the Deceived to be enjoyable to play but I want the Arisen to be even more enjoyable.<br /> <br /> One thing that does annoy me a lot are the <i>Mummy</i> supplements talking about things being revealed in future supplements that seem to do with the initial supplement's topic at hand. WW/OP has always disdained referring to Supplement A in Supplement B's text, unless it was in a side-bar. For example, in <i>Guildhalls of the Deathless</i> there's a side-bar mentioning that a future supplement will explore what happens when a shuankhsen eats a talisman; and in <i>Cursed Necropolis DC</i> a side-bar mentions that relic locations will be handled in the future, too.<br /> <br /> But...I don't get it! These books were your one chance to talk about these topics. When future books come out they won't want to write about talisman-eating shuankhsen or relic locations in DC because it's a supplement referring to another supplement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T13:09:08-07:00","id":126088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=126036#post126036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts on CN: DC in no particular order:<br /> <br /> * Unfortunately, this book has a lot of one of my biggest gripes about Mummy: lots of awesome weirdness going on the the fluff and the plot and <i>no rules for it</i><i>.</i> Geomancy, mirages and oases, Dedwen, ritual magic apparently unconnected to Affinities and Utterances, the list goes on.I want systems for creating my own geomantic effects! I want heka and Dedwen and the Word to be actual <i>things</i> with rules of their own, not just Guild-specific flavoring for the mechanics we already have! It's really frustrating to have all this cool, unique stuff in the descriptions and no way to <i>use</i> it more concrete than handwaving. I <i>really</i> hope that we'll see at least some of this in a future supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the book outright states that more details/rules for at least Oases/Mirages and &quot;Relic Buildings/Areas&quot; (which I presume is the result of Geomancy and will be something the Tef-Aabhi and Su-Mennet are likely tied to/involved with) are going to be in future books. So that's something.<br /> <br /> As for the ritual magic that's not obviously Affinities or Utterances, from everything I read that seems to be the stuff the Deceived can do. Which is likely to be covered in their own splat book. Though I am very stoked that the Deceived do seem to have some form of distinct magic from their Arisen cousins.<br /> <br /> (As an additional point in general with the Arisen and magic, everything the Arisen do with magic is preconstructed in some fashion. Mainly because the Shan'Iatu made sure the Guilds and Arisen only had half the picture when it comes to actually doing magic. They have the rote abilities of magic, but none of the underlying principles, so they can't actually alter/create anything new. All they can do is find preexisting stuff that set in a particular way. They lack &quot;the Will&quot; to do any of this stuff, but the Deceived have access to that sort of thing apparently.)<br /> <br /> This is why Deceived magic was involved in Washington and the White Jackels quest, because he realized that the basic magics the Tef-Aahbi (or any other the 5 guilds for that matter) had was not able to achieve what he wanted.<br /> <br /> As for Dedwen and Heka. I've always taken them as philosophical/theological theorem attached to the idea of magic by the Mesen-Nebu and Tef-Aahbi. They are ideas of how magic works and it makes sense for the Mummy's of those guilds to express their observations of those magics in those terms.<br /> <br /> I take all the talk in DC about &quot;heka&quot; flowing around the city as very much the theoretical viewpoint of the Tef-Aahbi and other Arisen influenced by them take. I believe it even mentions that a person using Godsight to view DC's skyline from a tall building will see Sekhem flowing around the city, but no mention of &quot;seeing&quot; Heka is made. Because heka is an idea, a mental construct to explain how the geomantic works in DC channel Sekhem around the city or channels mortals emotional resonance and perception around the Beltway (something that I believe the Guild Utterance for the Tef Aabhi can do in general).<br /> <br /> \u200bI will admit however, that depending on the writer the line between &quot;heka/dedwen is a thing&quot; and &quot;heka/dedwen&quot; is a concept/idea does seem to bounce around a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One thing that does annoy me a lot are the <i>Mummy</i> supplements talking about things being revealed in future supplements that seem to do with the initial supplement's topic at hand. WW/OP has always disdained referring to Supplement A in Supplement B's text, unless it was in a side-bar. For example, in <i>Guildhalls of the Deathless</i> there's a side-bar mentioning that a future supplement will explore what happens when a shuankhsen eats a talisman; and in <i>Cursed Necropolis DC</i> a side-bar mentions that relic locations will be handled in the future, too.<br /> <br /> But...I don't get it! These books were your one chance to talk about these topics. When future books come out they won't want to write about talisman-eating shuankhsen or relic locations in DC because it's a supplement referring to another supplement </div> </div> </div>Yeah this is an anomaly that seems specific to <i>Mummy</i> and its weird and slightly annoying. Personally I blame the page limit on the Core book.<br /> <br /> Its put me off running Mummy until all the supplements we currently have on the schedule are out because I want the 100% picture on everything before I try and run this game again.<br /> <br /> I think relic locations/oasis will be covered in Sothis, that's just a guess though (could be in Deceived). The Shuankhsen eating a talisman I suspect ties into the Avarice Chronicle that's running across the three major splat books. So it will likely be in Sothis too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Book of the Deceived</i> will have rules for playing the Sixth Guild, so you may be able to just play a heroic Deceived. All I can hope for is that, while the Deceived surely have some anti-hero motivations and justifications, they don't overshadow the typical Arisen. They might know more Secret Truths than the latter, but I don't want them to know everything. It's a fine line, but I want the Deceived to be enjoyable to play but I want the Arisen to be even more enjoyable. </div> </div> </div>I would not hate it if the Deceived stood equal with the Arisen in justification, motivation and I think its pretty clear they know a fair bit more then the Arisen about the &quot;truth&quot; or &quot;big picture&quot; of whats going on. Lets face it, anyone who's read the Storyteller section knows the Arisen are far from being in the &quot;right&quot; about most things. If its anything like the Brood book for Requiem 1.0 it will likely make the Deceived more compelling in certain aspects then the Arisen.<br /> <br /> In general if I had to say anyone one/group in the Mummy setting had the whole story of the deal with Irem, the Shan'Iatu and Duat I'd bet on the Heretic personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T13:15:32-07:00","id":126096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=126061#post126061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I half-agree on the first point. A lot of interesting stories and plots come from exceptions to the rules. Mummies can't be possessed by ephemeral beings so...what happens when that actually happens? The upcoming <i>Mage</i> update, <i>The Fallen World Chronicles</i>, posits just such Mysteries as the reason Mages even come together as a society in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree that leaving some things mysterious and undefined is good. The thing is, the stuff that's best left mysterious and undefined is just that--<i>mysterious.</i> What I'm objecting to isn't so much that there aren't rules for geomancy et al, but rather that it reads as if it <i>should</i> have rules support. It's not treated as a strange and inexplicable wonder, but as a great achievement within a well-known discipline--like the Eiffel Tower is to architecture.<br /> <br /> And the PCs are ostensibly architects, to stretch the metaphor, but the game is telling them that no, they can't actually plan or build stuff, they just theme everything they do around architecture without actually <i>doing</i> it. Except when the Storyteller needs a cool set piece, in which case it's all a matter of narration with no real control given to the players.<br /> <br /> It's the tabletop equivalent of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CutscenePowerToTheMax\" target=\"_blank\">Cutscene Power to the Max</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":743,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","user":"Exploding Frogs","date":". 05-05-2014, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T14:11:43-07:00","id":126131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=126096#post126096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I agree that leaving some things mysterious and undefined is good. The thing is, the stuff that's best left mysterious and undefined is just that--<i>mysterious.</i> What I'm objecting to isn't so much that there aren't rules for geomancy et al, but rather that it reads as if it <i>should</i> have rules support. It's not treated as a strange and inexplicable wonder, but as a great achievement within a well-known discipline--like the Eiffel Tower is to architecture.<br /> <br /> And the PCs are ostensibly architects, to stretch the metaphor, but the game is telling them that no, they can't actually plan or build stuff, they just theme everything they do around architecture without actually <i>doing</i> it. Except when the Storyteller needs a cool set piece, in which case it's all a matter of narration with no real control given to the players.<br /> <br /> It's the tabletop equivalent of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CutscenePowerToTheMax\" target=\"_blank\">Cutscene Power to the Max</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again to reiterate a point I made in my previous point in regards to this issue. <br /> <br /> Its not that the NPC's can do stuff the PC's can't with Geomancy. DC outright says that The White Jackel only managed to achieve the effects he has (and hopes for) with the DC nome because he's got hold of some Deceived Magic. Its just that he's managed to blag that he's pulled this off with a mastery of Geomancy and the aid of the other 4 Guilds knowledge (in particular the Mesen Nebu's Alchemy and the Sesha-Hesbu's mastery of the Word). <br /> <br /> Likewise, he's had the dream of Irem Reborn since the first Sothic Turn and has been working towards it since at least the 3rd Sothic Turn for EVERY ONE OF THIS DESCENTS there after (thats 1,400 odd years of Descents from an Arisen with a very active cult). If a player came to me with that background for a character I'd be happy to throw some interesting stuff their way e.g. realizing certain facts about Arisen magic, and having to make deals/getting manipulated without knowing it. Most PC's in experiences don't have that sort of character focus on large scale projects. <br /> <br /> In a more general sense,the idea that Geomancy can achieve unique effects is not actually stated anywhere in Mummy. Its presented an an underlying concept of how the Tef-Aahbi believe heka can be concentrated an manipulated, but heka is itself merely an idea to explain certain effects one might have on the world with hard work. The geomantic affinities and utterances to have some unique effects that benefit the Mummy and those the Mummy favours. In the latter's case its usually a method of accelerating or simplifying mundane activities. <br /> <br /> In general that's just he idea of &quot;good design&quot; taken to a mystical level, which is pretty much what the Tef-Aahbi are all about. <br /> <br /> I used to have the same hang-up on the issue of the Su-Mennet not having separate ritualized magic because their are priests. Until I realized the point I made previously about all Arisen magic being Rote. The Shan'Iatu made sure that all the abilities of the Arisen they intended were Affinities, and Utterances are but the smallest fraction (containing only the &quot;doing&quot; part of magic, rather then the base principles) the least of their Magic. The Shan'Iatu made sure the Arisen were limited, shacked to the purpose their were created for in very particular ways so that the Arisen developed and worked along lines dictated by them. Allowing their servants the ability to create wondrous effects not envisioned in their own plans would go directly against this. <br /> <br /> Hence they made sure that while a Tef-Aahbi could play with the loose concepts of heka/geomancy he would never know enough of the base metaphysics of magic to actually control/create with it. At best he has the set patterns of the heka/geomancy related affinities and utterances. The Tef-Aahbi can follow his base ideas about the way heka/geomancy work to try and do something original, but at best he's going to be able to maybe prove a theoretical point, never actually create something new. This is not the Rite of Return removing that knowledge or anything, the point is the Tef-Aahbi, even when they were a mortal guild in the city of Irem, never had all the base principles to do that sort of thing. The Shan'Iatu were very, very particular about keeping the base principles of magic away from their servants. <br /> <br /> As a metaphor think of a person working on a Car construction line. One group of guys that bolt the gear-boxes together. They know how to do that and they have enough knowledge of gear-boxes that they can fit them on many different models of car. They don't know how to make gear-boxes though. They could have a go at designing one from the fact they handle gear-boxes so much, but since they don't completely understand how it functions (only that it needs to function just-so to fit with the rest of the gear system) their chances of getting it right are pretty low to say the least. <br /> <br /> The Tef-Aahbi are those gear-box guys. The gearbox is idols/geomancy. The self-designed gearbox is their playing around with the ideas of heka/geomancy. The guys making the gearbox and have actually designed ones that worked/invented the gear-box are the Shan'Iatu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T16:24:56-07:00","id":126232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=126036#post126036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts on CN: DC in no particular order:<br /> <br /> * Back in the Guildhalls adventure, Bes-Mat should have had way more screentime than he did. (Or will have, from an in-universe perspective.) He's a much cooler character in here than the bland conservative Maa-Kep security guy who just hung out in the background, being overshadowed by pretty much everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this was written after Guildhalls, and I was given explicit instructions to feature Bes-Mat specifically, but I didn't have anything else to go on other than &quot;he's conservative&quot;, &quot;he's a friend to the Su-Menent&quot; and &quot;he moonlights as security.&quot;<br /> <br /> At the same time, I said to myself, &quot;I really need to work in the conservative guy who greets foreign Arisen because he's sufficiently toeing the line of the Judges that everyone can agree on him, oh and also he escorts them around in a food truck serving Iremite street food to boost Memory through tasty, tasty Sebayt,&quot; and, &quot;I need a Su-Menent Envoy as a cog in Sedge's Machine,&quot; and, &quot;Man, the Sons of Anarchy would make a really badass cult.&quot;<br /> <br /> So that's how Bes-Mat happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Unfortunately, this book has a lot of one of my biggest gripes about Mummy: lots of awesome weirdness going on the the fluff and the plot and <i>no rules for it</i><i>.</i> Geomancy, mirages and oases, Dedwen, ritual magic apparently unconnected to Affinities and Utterances, the list goes on.I want systems for creating my own geomantic effects! I want heka and Dedwen and the Word to be actual <i>things</i> with rules of their own, not just Guild-specific flavoring for the mechanics we already have! It's really frustrating to have all this cool, unique stuff in the descriptions and no way to <i>use</i> it more concrete than handwaving. I <i>really</i> hope that we'll see at least some of this in a future supplement. </div> </div> </div>The rules for Al-Wahat were lamentably and accidentally cut. But at any rate, I don't have room to describe the full potency and purview of the Washington Monument, nor do I have the proper tools to do so without constraining future writers. I, too, hope we'll see the Monument as an example of relic architecture<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Hebeny is awesome. That is all. </div> </div> </div>I spent a lot of time on Hebeny making sure he came off as realistic and not a token. Thank you very much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Speaking of Hebeny, I note that both he and Seb-Hetchet have the requisite Memory and Pillars to attempt Apotheosis, at least if the lowered Pillar requirements are in effect. Hints for future metaplot? </div> </div> </div>NWoD doesn't have metaplot, and I'm not sure if Hebeny or Seb-Hetchet will appear in future supplements.<br /> <br /> As for the Apotheosis requirements? All I'm gonna say is good catch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * I'd never considered that the Talismanic Record could serve as a poor man's Memory, but as written, it totally could. Interesting. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it's the only way nome structures and guilds function as social constructs. That, and cults doing their masters' bidding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Also, still no clear indication that the Deceived are actually evil. For all that the book demonizes them when talking about them from the perspective of the Arisen, the actual description of what Hab-Utet is trying to do is pretty ambiguous. I mean, he's described as wanting to &quot;tear down the works of Irem&quot;, but given what we know about what Irem was like, that's not exactly an inherently malevolent goal. (I mean, let's face it: in the world of Mummy, no one's hands are clean, and killing a few endangered animals to make a super-Amkhata is actually pretty tame as apparently &quot;evil&quot; acts go. The ostensible &quot;good guys&quot; in this scenario have done much, much worse.) I'm getting the impression that it would be entirely possible to play a heroic Deceived, even if Hab-Utet turns out to be evil incarnate. </div> </div> </div>Part of the frustrating thing as an author was trying to do a citybook before the line was fully mature. It's unavoidable, and to some degree, every line with a city book has suffered from this: New Orleans, Boston, and the Rockies all came around as one of the first supplements in their lines. Relic architecture, as above, but the Deceived are another element. The book clearly benefited from Guildhalls, though - Harry and I were able to grasp talismanic records as the main mechanism for nome life, the Flesh Masons make an appearance, you got to see Guildmasters exercising their full power, etc.<br /> <br /> In my case, I knew a good deal about the Deceived, but there was only so much I could hint at or describe. I did my best to ensure that the book would be just as useful after the Deceived book came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-05-2014, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T16:41:20-07:00","id":126245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=125215#post125215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the Monument is supposed to be finished in its repairs on the 12th of May 2014 (10 days from now) I was wondering if it has a different effect on the Arisen inside the beltway when fully repaired?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Monument has a number of powers accessible to anyone in the city, but it mainly exists to dampen Sybaris, regulate the flows that allow for a slowed Descent, and provide a unifying pillar to active the Rite of Irem. These things are hampered by the damage to the Monument, but they're not actually stopped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T19:18:09-07:00","id":126350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=126232#post126232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for Al-Wahat were lamentably and <b>accidentally </b>cut. But at any rate, I don't have room to describe the full potency and purview of the Washington Monument, nor do I have the proper tools to do so without constraining future writers. I, too, hope we'll see the Monument as an example of relic architecture</div> </div> </div> </div>Accidentally? Is there any chance they can accidentally be put back in? <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=126245#post126245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Monument has a number of powers accessible to anyone in the city, but it mainly exists to dampen Sybaris, regulate the flows that allow for a slowed Descent, and provide a unifying pillar to active the Rite of Irem. These things are hampered by the damage to the Monument, but they're not actually stopped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, dampening Sybaris - something we all were interested in figuring out, and Scutarii was looking for up-thread. Thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T20:50:55-07:00","id":126423,"title":"","content":"I second reseru's point here.<br /> <br /> Even if the majority of the Monuments extra powers get covered in another splat-book (which feels really odd to me, and slightly wrong, but I can understand the need for it) when the line fully covers Relic Architecture I would love it if you could put the anti-sybaris effects back in somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T05:25:33-07:00","id":126627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=123164#post123164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had something in there to deal with Unease Sybaris and how they interact with nomes; it appears to have slipped out, so I'll see if I can't get it put back in. I realize you don't find the answer particularly palatable, Christian, but the answer to &quot; how do guild and nomes even work with no memory&quot; is &quot;cults and talismans&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any possibility of posting it here (unless its a large amount of text). Im currently running a chronicle in DC and this info would be handy.<br /> <br /> Excellent, excellent book Neall, outstanding addition to the Mummy line <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T19:14:05-07:00","id":127167,"title":"","content":"I'll see, folks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T18:48:18-07:00","id":129484,"title":"","content":"Was it included in the latest pdf update sent today?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T21:13:44-07:00","id":129592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=129484#post129484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it included in the latest pdf update sent today?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; last page of the ST chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T22:48:29-07:00","id":129637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=129592#post129592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah; last page of the ST chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its an awesome rule that provides a much more wide-spanning benefit to vestiges in general.<br /> <br /> While their three things they helped with before (resorting pillars, resurrection and calling) were useful abilities they only really came up during specific events I did still have players asking why they would want a vestige over a relic.<br /> <br /> In fact its such a good rule that I actually wish it had been in the Corebook. As it makes vestiges so much more important and explains why Nomes in big cities (particularly capitals and famous cities) can work and are in fact actually a good idea for the Arisen to congregate to. <br /> <br /> I have a question Neall, with the way the part about the Monument works in relation to Unease Sybaris.<br /> <br /> Does that mean that any city with a monument of substantial fame have a similar affect for Mummy's in another city?<br /> <br /> For example the Eiffel Tower in Paris or the Statue of Liberty in New York acting as general &quot;vestiges&quot; for the city to negate some Sybaris effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T04:26:30-07:00","id":129784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=129592#post129592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; last page of the ST chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for getting this in for us; you're my new hero. A side-bar mentioned rules for mirages later in the book and it was pretty disorienting to then not see said rule. I do like the bit about vestiges dampening unease sybaris. The Lifeweb side-bar in the core did seem to be hinting at something more complex and integrated, and I'm glad to see it fleshed out a bit more.<br /> <br /> I gotta say honestly, though, that I hope not every nome is so dependent on dampening unease sybaris. Why would they want to? It's a domino effect that benefits them in the long-term: awaken, cause sybaris which influences people to join cults, recruit those mortals to your cult, awaken more often because your cult basically gets bigger every time you're in a Descent, profit! So while I see the usefulness of the effects and the unique situation with the Washington Monument, I hope it's an exceptional circumstance and not how Mummies get by.Plus, sybaris in such huge amounts really only happens during a Sothic turn, of which there have been <b>four</b> compared to the <b>dozens</b> of Descents <b>each</b> Mummy has had. In those 'off-seasons' there's certainly less reason to keep sybaris in check<br /> <br /> I hope we see a setting (Rio? Cursed Necropolis Tokyo?!) where sybaris is completely rampant and out of control - maybe as an exceptional circumstance of the other end of the spectrum, but that would be a compelling playground, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T09:41:05-07:00","id":129931,"title":"","content":"So wait, where are the rules for vestiges dampening or overwriting unease sybaris, because I don't know that I've seen them anywhere. Yet they're referenced in the mirage sidebar and referred to like they're a known thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T10:51:52-07:00","id":129990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=129931#post129931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wait, where are the rules for vestiges dampening or overwriting unease sybaris, because I don't know that I've seen them anywhere. Yet they're referenced in the mirage sidebar and referred to like they're a known thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep in the updated version (released yesterday 9th) of DC the rules relating to Vestiges negating Unease Sybaris are detailed in a large sidebar on the last page of the Storytelling chapter (Chapter 4). <br /> <br /> To address the point reseru brings up - <br /> <br /> Controlled Sybaris is useful, because it allows the Arisen (and their Cult) to tailor the mindset and disposition of an area to something useful for the Mummy e.g. Cults against Death or Signs and Omens. As you say, such things are useful to make sure a Cult is maintained and finds easy recruits that it can grow by inducing into its ranks. <br /> <br /> The problem is uncontrolled Sybaris in an area. If people keep on having the Flood of Duat result a lot of &quot;odd stuff&quot; is going to start happening in an area. This draws mortal attention in a not-so-useful way. Cults are at their most effective when they are secret after all.<br /> <br /> Worse, anyone who knows about Mummy's such as Last Dynasty Inc (or several other Hunter compacts like the Ascended Ones or AKD) can be alerted and drawn to the area. Bringing real peril to the Arisen and their cult in a more immediate fashion.<br /> <br /> Its also worth noting that while its Sybaris is good for the recruitment drive and omens it might produce in mortal followers it also has a notably detrimental effect on sanity. Gibbering Cultists have their uses but you don't want your whole cult made up of them. <br /> <br /> For Nomes controlling Sybaris has to be an issue. If only one Arisen is around then the point you make about Sothic Turns and descents does apply, enough Arisen are not awakening close enough to one another most of the time for it to be an issue. However, in a Nome like DC with 24 Arisen who seem to be awaken fairly often even outside Sothic turns to guide their Cults, Sybaris would be happening more often then is healthy for the Nomes mortal population. Hence the need for things like a steady flow of Vestiges in the city to anchor to Lifewebs and monuments to bleed away Sybaris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T10:56:31-07:00","id":129998,"title":"","content":"No, I'm looking at the last page of chapter 4 of what (unless the download messed up on me) should be the updated book. The sidebar labelled &quot;of monuments and mirages&quot;? It only references vestiges negating sybaris in passing, and then goes on into the rules for how the monument in particular works and how mirages (aka the magical side effects of using one big vestige to cancel everyone's sybaris at once) function.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for the rule that's being referenced in that sidebar. How does vestiges cancelling sybaris work in normal, non-washington-monument situations, and where is it detailed?<br /> <br /> Edit: wait, nevermind, I just noticed the tiny parenthetical where it's explained. <i>Wow</i> that should really be in the core somewhere. Anyway, ignore me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 05-10-2014, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T11:35:47-07:00","id":130029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=129998#post129998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: wait, nevermind, I just noticed the tiny parenthetical where it's explained. <i>Wow</i> that should really be in the core somewhere. Anyway, ignore me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I had to read the sidebar about three times to get it all clear in my head. The normal vestige rules for Sybaris cancellation are about 2 sentences (one in parenthesize).<br /> <br /> Then it goes into rules that imply any adequately sized monument that hold or did hold a large amount of emotional resonance in any city e.g. Nelson Column in London can have an effect that means it negates a certain degree of Unease Sybaris effects from any Arisen in the city.<br /> <br /> Finally it mentions how due to Washington unique geomantic design interacting with the Monument (which is basically a giant Vestige for the city as detailed in the sidebar and also possibly a Relic Architecture which will be detailed in a future book) means that it also produces Mirages. So I've read it that not every &quot;city vestige&quot; produces these effects, they are unique to DC. <br /> <br /> Also yes, the ability for Vestiges to control/moderate Sybaris really, really should have been in the Corebook as another use for them on top of the listed 3 in the core. Considering the Lifeweb even had a sidebar specifically about anchoring Relics and Vestiges it would have fit right in.<br /> <br /> Still it would not be the first time a WoD game had important rules pushed into a splat book and I'm glad we have the rules now with DC. Something for them to definitely include in the core if they do a Mummy Chronicle book in the next couple of years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T15:16:13-07:00","id":130364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=129990#post129990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To address the point reseru brings up - <i>snip</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, all fair enough. I just hope it isn't standard for Mummy cities. It's a storytelling tool, not a burden. If it draws monster/cult hunters to the area then it's a story, which is why you're playing the game, you know? To tell interesting stories","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T16:25:03-07:00","id":130947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=129592#post129592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah; last page of the ST chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet!! Just found it :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T00:44:10-07:00","id":131759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=130364#post130364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, all fair enough. I just hope it isn't standard for Mummy cities. It's a storytelling tool, not a burden. If it draws monster/cult hunters to the area then it's a story, which is why you're playing the game, you know? To tell interesting stories</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see you point. I have mixed feelings on Sybaris and its place in the game.<br /> <br /> I think it provides a great in-game reason for the ability of Scorpion Cults to recruit and how a Mummy sorta channels extra-dimensional energy. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, its all a little on-the-nose for me. I think I would prefer it to be more like Disquiet in Promethean, where it starts off as a very subtle effect and builds up among those you have more contact with. So your Cultists are getting the Omens and Dreams and such. Normal people on the street are just getting the creeps a little unless you get tangled up in their lives. At the moment Sybaris is less like Disquiet in this regard and more like Lunacy (though that parallel only really applies to terror Sybaris). <br /> <br /> Also my experiences with Sybaris in game as an ST have been a bit mixed. My players viewed it either as an inherently &quot;bad thing&quot; like Disquiet to mitigate to its lower levels. As a contradiction to this they also often tried to argue that it applied to pretty much every social interaction the Arisen had with mortals and should mean X or Y or Z (where any of these values are helping them get what they want).<br /> <br /> Maybe if I ran Mummy again and was a little bit more on the ball with Sybaris and my players were a little bit more on-board with it I could come to like it more. At current it part of the game I'd try to minimize if I ran the game again. So the new vestige rules are pretty much perfect for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T17:25:26-07:00","id":132926,"title":"","content":"I like some aspects of Sybaris better than Disquiet.. namely, the timing, the restriction to touching the mummy/talking to it, its tomb, etc. I felt like Sybaris has fewer downsides than disquiet, doesn't hit as often, doesn't affect other monsters, etc. I have a feeling the Promethean chronicle book might make disquiet more like Sybaris, or handle it like Ive heard they did in Mortal Remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T18:41:14-07:00","id":133028,"title":"","content":"I reread the sybaris rules, and really I don't think unease sybaris is that bad.<br /> <br /> If you've never been in the Mummy's tomb, never interacted with the Mummy or its relics itself, or never encounter one of its cultists while the Mummy is awake then the effects are one step lower (meaning, less intense/powerful). Considering that unease sybaris is directly correlated to the Mummy's sekhem, the degree of sybaris will go down an entire step after the first day, more or less. Then over the course of its descent, the sybaris will not only become less intense but the radius will decrease accordingly, too.<br /> <br /> So imagine it. The Mummy awakens, some people near its tomb get depressed for a couple days, maybe someone scrawls some Iremite gibberish in a back alley, and then things return to relative normalcy. In a hypothetical person's diary, it's just a couple entries where they say, &quot;Dear Diary, today I felt like crap. What's the point of living because life doesn't last forever?&quot; Then a few days later they reread their diary and think, &quot;Yeah, I don't know what got into me. I was just in a weird mood&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T06:26:11-07:00","id":133633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=130364#post130364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, all fair enough. I just hope it isn't standard for Mummy cities. It's a storytelling tool, not a burden. If it draws monster/cult hunters to the area then it's a story, which is why you're playing the game, you know? To tell interesting stories</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes you don't want to tell the story with Sybaris so providing rules and sch for removing it are a useful addition as far as I am concerned. Sometime showever you DO want it and if there are already ways of reducing it then it's not a huge stretch of the imagination that similar things could be used to increase the effects.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T12:31:16-07:00","id":134223,"title":"","content":"I'm just dropping in because I've noticed a tendency to exaggerate some of the difficulties of Memory and Sybaris, and as the designer of both I'd like to point the following out:<br /> <br /> 1) At Memory 3 (see p. 78) you know your guild, decree and in rough terms, your last Descent. To clarify, &quot;knowing&quot; your guild (or decree) means more than seeing the word &quot;Su-Menent&quot; on the back of your hand--you know what it is to be a member of this guild. Your mind also possesses information you have learned from others and experienced yourself, but you have trouble weaving them into a coherent narrative, or telling the difference between secondhand knowledge and experience. There are blackouts at points where your Memory may have been higher (so you don't &quot;remember remembering&quot;) but by and large, you're a fair bit better off than Guy Pearce in Memento, though for various reasons you might make the same mistakes by, for instance, misremembering a rumour of someone plotting against you as having *witnessed* this plot. But this does mean that yes, mummies can form coherent social structures. It's only at Memory 1, when conscious knowledge of the guild is lost, that organization is impossible--though at 2, when the mummy *is* operating at Memento level, it gets tough.<br /> <br /> 2) A typical Arisen generates an Unease Sybaris of -7 (3-10) at the start of his Descent--no more than that! That's why the rules specify -8 at the point where the people go, as the ancient necromancers put it, kind of apeshit. -7 to -5 kind of casts a Gothic pall over the mummy's surroundings. People find refuge from a sense of nihilism in church and state, and mummies, who sort of represent *both* in an occult sense, enjoy a bit of an edge. But crazygonuts scrawling in inspired Iremite really happens when Memory 2 or less Arisen come back. People may unconsciously insert the odd King in Yellow-like reference into cricket bat spankings and other closed society initiations, but it's the kind of thing that would pass casual scrutiny.<br /> <br /> So in short, to have a bunch of mummies hanging out in an organized fashion you don't absolutely need special gimmicks, though it does help. The rules are specifically designed to permit a certain degree of social organization for mummies and for the most part, make mortals act strange within the parameters of a &quot;modern Gothic&quot; atmosphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T00:52:49-07:00","id":135093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=134223#post134223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just dropping in because I've noticed a tendency to exaggerate some of the difficulties of Memory and Sybaris, and as the designer of both I'd like to point the following out:<br /> <br /> 1) (Memory &amp; Guilds)<br /> <br /> 2) (Sybaris)<br /> <br /> So in short, to have a bunch of mummies hanging out in an organized fashion you don't absolutely need special gimmicks, though it does help. The rules are specifically designed to permit a certain degree of social organization for mummies and for the most part, make mortals act strange within the parameters of a &quot;modern Gothic&quot; atmosphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for saying eloquently what I've been saying all along. Even when I read <i>Guildhalls of the Deathless</i>, the application of talismans as a 'detached memory encyclopedia' didn't really occur to me. It's kind of silly to think all along that the writers would've laid the groundwork for 'the most political of all the splats' (said somewhere in the early pages of the core) and then not line that up with the default level of Memory. I can see how, but eh, hindsight I guess? So, thanks for the extra clarification! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Like I said above, while I like the extra bit about vestiges and appreciate them being re-added into <i>DC</i>, I like sybaris the way it is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T10:57:27-07:00","id":135529,"title":"","content":"I'm really surprised at how many people did not think of talismans alongside the entire &quot;detached memory repository&quot; lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T11:27:40-07:00","id":135555,"title":"","content":"I did, I quite simply find the idea of a great deal of a mummy's memory being stored in a relic to be not that interesting.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for putting things into context, Malcolm!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T16:34:57-07:00","id":147274,"title":"","content":"does Cursed Necropolis have rules for political elections? they where metioned in the rise and fall theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T18:43:42-07:00","id":149901,"title":"","content":"I've enjoyed the book tremendously so far, but one thing struck me as worth mentioning. For a species of immortals beset by a number of supernatural enemies, including those interested in the grisly and repeated consumption of their flesh in exchange for greater power, the Arisen of DC display a remarkable dearth of capacity for protecting themselves. One assumes that this is being left to their cults for the most part (though how secure this is against the Shaunksen is unclear). Where evidence is available of the capacity to have it out with an opponent, it tends to be haphazard, with a token nod to combat ability absent much support. The only ones who tend to break the mold do so because of an unusual overall amount of capacity in all facets of the character, and combat simply seems to benefit from this (Sedge and the Jackal come to mind). One example in particular has an Arisen with the Guardian Wrath affinity and no brawl skill. Am I missing something about how they function in their environment? Does the Jackal come out to play every time a Shaunksen stalks the city? Are the cults key to combating supernatural threats in a way that hasn't been discussed? They've always struck me more as an Arisen's interface with the mortal world, than a monster squad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T17:24:32-07:00","id":150906,"title":"","content":"Since this is a book that has been created post GMC, is it GMC compliant? I remember OP saying that every book that comes out after GMC comes out with the revised rules set. So i'm crossing my fingers on this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T17:34:23-07:00","id":150912,"title":"","content":"Mummy is the exception to the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T00:36:07-07:00","id":151097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>willywonka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=149901#post149901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've enjoyed the book tremendously so far, but one thing struck me as worth mentioning. For a species of immortals beset by a number of supernatural enemies, including those interested in the grisly and repeated consumption of their flesh in exchange for greater power, the Arisen of DC display a remarkable dearth of capacity for protecting themselves. One assumes that this is being left to their cults for the most part (though how secure this is against the Shaunksen is unclear). Where evidence is available of the capacity to have it out with an opponent, it tends to be haphazard, with a token nod to combat ability absent much support. The only ones who tend to break the mold do so because of an unusual overall amount of capacity in all facets of the character, and combat simply seems to benefit from this (Sedge and the Jackal come to mind). One example in particular has an Arisen with the Guardian Wrath affinity and no brawl skill. Am I missing something about how they function in their environment? Does the Jackal come out to play every time a Shaunksen stalks the city? Are the cults key to combating supernatural threats in a way that hasn't been discussed? They've always struck me more as an Arisen's interface with the mortal world, than a monster squad.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on this is that the guilds are primarily comprised of artisans, so as a culture they're likely less prone to focus on combat. Despite that, when a threat arises any mummy can charge their sahu with Sekhem to become a nigh-unstoppable monstrosity, at least at high levels of Sekhem. They don't need natural ability when they have a pool of unnatural power at their disposal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T22:25:43-07:00","id":158729,"title":"","content":"I really appreciated the book being written by locals, the write-ups on the city itself FEEL like DC. (Including the general disdain for WMATA)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T10:04:18-07:00","id":159166,"title":"","content":"I love the fact that Meridian Hill Park and the Kenilworth Aquatic Gardens are such a big deal; they're both pretty fantastic places in real life. Lots of love for the 495 hatred, particularly around the Mixing Bowl. It makes total sense that the Beltway generates demons; that's the only possible explanation for all the overturned cars on fire you hear about around Dale City.<br /> <br /> I would have liked more info on the Maryland parts of the DC area (Silver Spring for the win), but you can't have everything. Also, maybe some discussion on how you really shouldn't try to drive in certain parts of DC unless you know exactly where you're going. Go ahead, try to navigate through the Tidal Basin area relying on your smart phone map. You'll wind up in Arlington before you know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T08:50:11-07:00","id":161776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=150906#post150906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this is a book that has been created post GMC, is it GMC compliant? I remember OP saying that every book that comes out after GMC comes out with the revised rules set. So i'm crossing my fingers on this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not. Mummy the Curse is not going to be GMC compatible, and it was never intended to be. <b>Mummy is a core nWOD system game</b>. Nothing stops you from converting it (lots of mashups on this site, just search). I for one am very happy its not GMC.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T22:28:50-07:00","id":163174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123107-cursed-necropolis-dc-discussion?p=161776#post161776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is not. Mummy the Curse is not going to be GMC compatible, and it was never intended to be. <b>Mummy is a core nWOD system game</b>. Nothing stops you from converting it (lots of mashups on this site, just search). I for one am very happy its not GMC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious, why are you happy it's not GMC?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T06:14:48-07:00","id":163495,"title":"","content":"I actually enjoy WOD system as is. It is not to say that I dont enjoy playing GMC, but I dont feel compelled to translate everything over to it. I can enjoy a game of Mummy under the existing core rules and I can equally enjoy a game of Demon which is written under GMC. <br /> <br /> IMO nWOD system is still one of the best game systems around, and I plan on playing and running for many years to come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}